                    <li><span className="bg-green-200/60 px-1 rounded-sm">sage</span> — grounded, systemic, ecological</li>
                    <li><span className="bg-blue-200/60 px-1 rounded-sm">blue</span> — analytical, definitional, precise</li>
                    <li><span className="bg-pink-200/60 px-1 rounded-sm">pink</span> — speculative, tender, soft hypothesis</li>
                    <li><span className="bg-orange-200/60 px-1 rounded-sm">orange</span> — urgent, open question, flag</li>
                    <li><span className="bg-gray-200/60 px-1 rounded-sm">gray</span> — aside, caveat, low-confidence</li>
                  </ul>
                  <p className="mt-2">highlights and underlines can be stacked on the same span — a highlighted, wavy-underlined phrase carries more semantic weight than either alone.</p>
                </>
              ),
            },
            {
              title: 'hyperlinks',
              body: (
                <>
                  <p>link any text span to a url. linked text is visually distinct (underlined, colored) and clickable in presentation mode or exports. useful for citations, references, or linking to external resources from within your diagram.</p>
                </>
              ),
            },
            {
              title: 'subscript & superscript',
              body: (
                <>
                  <p>toggle subscript or superscript on any text selection. useful for chemical formulas (H₂O), mathematical notation (x²), footnote markers, and academic references.</p>
                </>
              ),
            },
            {
              title: 'redact',
              body: (
                <>
                  <p>a filled opaque bar over the text — for censored content, placeholders, or that redacted-document aesthetic. the underlying text is still there, just visually hidden. useful for mockups, privacy-sensitive diagrams, or dramatic effect.</p>
                </>
              ),
            },
          ],
        },
        {
          title: 'text styles',
          body: (
            <>
              <p>save any combination of formatting — font, size, weight, color, highlight, underline style, underline color — as a named text style. apply it to any text span with one click from the styles drawer.</p>
              <p>set a default text style that applies to every new text annotation automatically. change the default and all future annotations inherit it — existing ones stay as they were.</p>
            </>
          ),
        },
      ]}
    />
  );
}

